#X obj 639 11 conv.midi2freq;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 236 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 The object converts a MIDI pitch (note number) into
a frequency in hertz \, with support for alternative reference pitches
(via the A argument or @a property) and historical temperaments (via
the @t property). Unlike the standard [mtof] object \, which always
uses 12-tone equal temperament with A4 = 440 Hz \, this object allows
you to choose a different reference pitch (for example \, 415 Hz for
Baroque tuning) or a different temperament.;
#X text 240 214 Supported temperaments: 'eq' (12-tone equal temperament)
\, 'just' (just intonation) \, 'ganassi' (Ganassi) \, 'meantone' (quarter-comma
meantone) \, 'kirnberger3' (Kirnberger III) \, 'pythagorean' (Pythagorean
tuning) \, 'rameau' (Rameau) \, 'valotti' (Vallotti) \, 'zarlino' (Zarlino).;
